{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03310388","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03310388","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* part of algae or fungus FOODON:03420247\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"torula yeast (dry)","obo_id":"FOODON:03310388","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03310554","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03310554","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* part of algae or fungus FOODON:03420247\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"brewers yeast (dry)","obo_id":"FOODON:03310554","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03302626","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03302626","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* not heat-treated FOODON:03440003\n* part of algae or fungus FOODON:03420247\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"yeast (fine, dry, active)","obo_id":"FOODON:03302626","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03306041","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03306041","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* whole animal or most parts used FOODON:03420173\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"yeast (fine, dry)","obo_id":"FOODON:03306041","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03310891","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03310891","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* whole animal or most parts used FOODON:03420173\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"yeast (fine, dry, inactive)","obo_id":"FOODON:03310891","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03307932","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03307932","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* whole animal or most parts used FOODON:03420173\n* smoked by adding smoke concentrate FOODON:03460110\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116"],"label":"torula yeast (artificially smoke-flavored, dried)","obo_id":"FOODON:03307932","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03540233","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03540233","description":["The group includes any type of dry pre-mixes containing flour, dried yeast and other ingredients used for the preparation of bread (usually home-made bread), after addition of a proper liquid. The part consumed/analysed is by default the whole or a portion of it representing the observed heterogeneity.[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking_mix] and [https://www.google.co.uk/search?tbm\u003disch\u0026q\u003dBread+premixes+]"],"label":"02330 - bread pre-mixes (dry) (efsa foodex2)","obo_id":"FOODON:03540233","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03307934","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03307934","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* finely ground FOODON:03430106\n* whole animal or most parts used FOODON:03420173\n* water removal process FOODON:03460138\n* smoked or smoke-flavored FOODON:03460172\n* preservation by dehydration or drying FOODON:03470116\n* ingredient: flavoring or taste ingredient added FOODON:03460117"],"label":"torula yeast (artificially bacon-flavored, smoked, dried)","obo_id":"FOODON:03307934","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001260","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00001260","description":["Beer is a fermented cereal beverage resulting from the fermentation most commonly of malted barley (though wheat, corn, or rice may included), by a yeast, most commonly Saccharomyces cerevisiae, and flavored by dried flowers of hops, Humulus lupulus."],"label":"beer beverage","obo_id":"FOODON:00001260","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03315109","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03315109","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* divided or disintegrated FOODON:03430122\n* dry mix FOODON:03530090\n* seed (anatomical part) FOODON:03420155"],"label":"baking mix (yeast leavened)","obo_id":"FOODON:03315109","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03315086","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03315086","description":["SIREN DB annotation:\n* disintegrated or ground FOODON:03430136\n* dry mix FOODON:03530090\n* seed (anatomical part) FOODON:03420155\n* carbohydrate fermentation process FOODON:03460256"],"label":"bakery product (yeast leavened, prepared mix)","obo_id":"FOODON:03315086","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400783","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400783","description":["Fermented milk is a milk product obtained by fermentation of milk, which milk may have been manufactured from products obtained from milk with or without compositional modification as limited by the provision in Section 3.3, by the action of suitable microorganisms and resulting in reduction of pH with or without coagulation (CODEX STAN 243-2003).  Fermented milk products include a range of foods commonly referred to as yogurt (or yoghurt), plus sour milk drinks produced by fermentation. A few of these are alcoholic as they are made with combined lactic and yeast ferments (e.g. kefir, koumiss); others are lactic fermented milk products (e.g. cieddu, kaeder milk, skyr, taette). In some traditional fermented milk products, such as Stragisto (strained yoghurt), Labneh, Ymer and Ylette, Milk the protein has been increased to minimum 5.6%.  ."],"label":"fermented milk product (eurofir)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400783","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_00001086","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_00001086","description":["A fermented milk drink made from  milk. It is prepared by inoculating cow, goat, or sheep\u0027s milk with kefir grains, a combination of bacteria and yeasts in a matrix of proteins, lipids, and sugars. This symbiotic matrix forms \"grains\" that resemble cauliflower. Many different bacteria and yeasts are found in the kefir grains, which are a complex and highly variable community of micro-organisms termed probiotics."],"label":"kefir food product","obo_id":"FOODON:00001086","type":"class"},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03311874","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03311874","description":["A fermented, slightly alcoholic, lightly effervescent, sweetened black or green tea drink commonly intended as a functional beverage for its supposed health benefits. It is called kombucha tea to distinguish it from the kombucha culture of bacteria and yeast.","SIREN DB annotation:\n* liquid FOODON:03430130\n* fully heat-treated FOODON:03440014\n* microbial/enzymatic modification process FOODON:03460119"],"label":"kombucha tea","obo_id":"FOODON:03311874","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["kombucha"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/FOODON_03400878","ontology_name":"foodon","ontology_prefix":"FOODON","short_form":"FOODON_03400878","description":["Includes any products that can be described/observed as alcoholic drink making supplies; extra or replacement components for alcohol making kits or components for home put together kits. These products are individual pieces of hardware such as, siphons and fermentation locks and separately packaged ingredients such as brewers yeast.  These products can either be disposable or re-usable. Excludes products such as Alcohol Making Kits and Pre-Made Alcohol."],"label":"10000143 - alcohol making supplies (gs1 gpc)","obo_id":"FOODON:03400878","type":"class"}],"numFound":15,"start":0},"responseHeader":{"QTime":0,"status":0},"facet_counts":{"facet_fields":{"ontologyPreferredPrefix":["FOODON","15"],"isDefiningOntology":["true","15"],"ontologyId":["foodon","15","cmo","7","mesh","4","hgnc","3","ncit","3","envo","2","hgnc.genegroup","2","slm","1","tfo","1","chebi","1","xco","1","enm","1","go","1","maxo","1","micro","1","omit","1","pr","1"],"ontologyIri":["http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/foodon.owl","15"],"isObsolete":["false","15"],"type":["class","15"]}}}